 "_doc": "Icon Kit themes. A class theme colours the PLATE (the stone behind the picture) so a mage's spells read blue/violet and a warrior's iron red-brown at a glance; an element theme colours the GLOW (and a tintable glyph). `tint` = plate colour (laid over the grey stone with the 'color' blend, at `strength`), `glow` = glow colour, `words` (elements) = name words that only say the element, so a match on them alone is flagged as an element fallback; `glyph` = the glyph used when a spell has no better match (the class's emblem / the element's picture). `frame` (classes) = the class-themed frame (data/layers.json frames) used when a spec asks for frame \"class\"; `dispel` = the inner-ring colour per dispel kind; `aliases` maps other games' class and element ids onto these. js/iconkit.js themeFor() is the one reader.",
